  "location": "Camp Wheeler, Ogdensburgh, N.Y.",
  "excerpt": "We reached here last Sat. and have been waiting for the Paymaster ever since. He has not come yet and I have some doubts whether I shall be able to be home this week.",
  "attribution": "Alexander, to his mother — Camp Wheeler, Ogdensburgh, N.Y. · July 27, 1865",
  "stem": "Home state reached, war over — and Alexander is stuck in camp because one official hasn’t arrived. Who is he waiting for?",
